<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Håkon Sigurdsson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 937–995</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Haakon Jarl, Haakon Sigurdsson, Hákon Sigurðarson</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Håkon Sigurdsson, known as Haakon Jarl, was Earl of Lade who ruled most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> from about 975 to 995 under the overlordship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-bluetooth">Harald Bluetooth</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, and later independently. A firm supporter of the old Norse gods, he defeated the Jomsvikings at the Battle of Hjörungavágr. He was killed in 995 as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olaf-tryggvason">Olaf Tryggvason</a> seized power in Norway.</p></div>
